 So you want to calculate 
$$\int_0^{\infty}  rac{1}{x}  rac{1}{2^{
u/2} \Gamma(
u/2)} x^{
u/2-1} e^{-x/2} dx = \int_0^{\infty}  rac{1}{2^{
u/2} \Gamma(
u/2)} x^{
u/2-2} e^{-x/2} dx.$$ 
 Rewrite the integrand so that it is the pdf of a $\chi^2(
u-2)$ random variable, which will then integrate to 1.  The leftover constant factor will be the expected value you're looking for. 
