Here's an argument based on l'Hôpital's rule: 
 $$
\begin{array}{rcl}
\lim_{u \to \infty} \int_0^1 f(ux) \, dx 
&\stackrel{\color{Brown}{ux = y}}{=}& \lim_{u \to \infty}\frac{\int_0^u f(y) \, dy}{u}
\\&\stackrel{\color{Brown}{\text{l'Hôpital}}}{=}& \lim_{u \to \infty} \frac{\frac{d}{du}\int_0^u f(y) \, dy}{\frac{d}{du}u} 
\\& \stackrel{\phantom{ux \to y}}{=}& \lim_{u \to \infty} f(u) 
\\&\stackrel{\phantom{ux \to y}}{=}& 0,
\end{array}
$$
since $u^2 f(u) \to 1$ as $u \to \infty$.  
